## Key Concepts & Terminology

### Glossary for Marketing

| Term | Simple Explanation | Marketing Usage |
|------|-------------------|-----------------|
| **Execution Engine** | Software that enforces rules during a process | "Isagawa is an execution engine for AI workflows" |
| **Domain Expertise** | Deep knowledge of a specific field (QA, API design, etc.) | "We encode domain expertise into software" |
| **Enforcement Layer** | The part that prevents AI from deviating | "Built-in enforcement — not suggestions" |
| **Design Decisions (DDs)** | The specific rules that define "correct" | "22 design decisions define professional QA standards" |
| **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** | How AI tools communicate with our engine | Don't use in marketing — too technical |
| **Workflow** | A multi-step process to complete a task | "Complex workflows executed correctly" |
| **Guardrails** | Boundaries that keep AI on track | "Guardrails for AI workflows" |
| **Human Escalation** | When AI stops and asks a human | "Knows when to ask for help" |

### Phrases to Use

**DO use:**
- "Execution engine" (our category)
- "Expert workflows"
- "The right way, every time"
- "Enforced, not suggested"
- "Consistent outcomes"
- "AI you can trust with critical work"

**DON'T use:**
- "AI assistant" (sounds like ChatGPT)
- "Copilot" (sounds like GitHub Copilot)
- "Automation tool" (sounds like Zapier)
- "No-code" (we're for technical users)

